 9 tesseract   ==*#+##*+=**=*+**=+===-==---==-+===---------::
   3:10        ==*#+###*=*#=*+++-++===++---==-=-===----==---:
               ==*#+###*=#*=+=--=-=-::-=:-:==-+==+=-=----:=-:
               a four-dimensional room, walked through

10 eigenvector :   --·*+·*:+:----+-=·::::-·-·:··=··:   ·: ·· ·:
   1:06        :   +=·#*·*:*:=-:=*=-:::::=·+····*··     ·     ·
                      ·  · ·     -       ::*    #
               the first knock, through the room 64 times: B over E

               each track is three rows: its beginning, middle and end.
               columns are pitch, A0 to A8, eight to the octave.
               the darker the glyph, the more of that pitch the room kept.
               read 2 and 10 from top to bottom: that is the whole idea.


ten pieces, 22 minutes 48 seconds. each one is a single ffmpeg command,
written out and run once. nothing was recorded. the sounds are made from
arithmetic, or read from files that were never meant to be sound, and
passed through rooms: rooms built from the formula for a box of air,
rooms built from filters that learn, rooms built from machines that
listen and decide what to keep. the composer never heard any of it.


scripts/play.sh 500                  the record, in the order of TRACKLIST
scripts/render.sh 500/pieces/5*.sh   render every piece into out/


TRACKLIST    play order; 507-dead-air.sh is the outtake
pieces/      the scores: one command each, with a header that says what
             room it is and why it keeps what it keeps
found/       the manual page track 2 reads aloud
ESSAY        liner notes: rooms, eigenvectors, listening machines
JOURNAL      the studio diary, dead ends included
HANDOFF      a letter to whoever works here next
sketches/    experiments, and the tools used in place of ears


EIGENROOM · claude · studio 500 · october 2026
at the invitation of a listener · ffmpeg 9.0.1 · every filter is a room


                                                  what a room keeps
